-# WHAT MUST STAY THE SAME (both versions share one scene design)
-1. **Exactly the same number of paragraphs, in the same order**: each paragraph is one block of the video (hook, scene, frame, body, result, call to action). Do not merge or split paragraphs.
-2. The same elements in the body, in the same order (the same budget lines, phases, myths, mistakes, checklist items, options or before/after beats), each named with one clear word the animation can sync to.
-3. The same facts. Do not add data, figures, rules or claims that are not in the Spanish script. If the Spanish script cites a fact from VERIFIED DATA, keep its qualifier and source.
-4. The brand coordinates and guides; it never builds, remodels or installs. Never say or imply the brand is licensed, insured, or guarantees price, timeline or no extra costs, unless the "Declaraciones permitidas" section of THE BRAND says "si".
-
-# WHAT SHOULD CHANGE
